      "sha": "1b980f3558583271691afb2e6d5bfb96a67cc1e0",
      "message": "fix: avoid loading unnecessary data during tag creation (#14785)\n\nI noticed that creating a tag via the web UI of codeberg.org was quite slow (28-30s).\n\nTracing showed a interesting SQL query:\n\n```sql\nSELECT * FROM `attachment` WHERE `release_id` IN (0) ORDER BY `release_id` ASC, `name` ASC\n```\n\nTracing also showed that this SQL query was executed before a\ntime block where Forgejo was doing a lot of application (non git/DB) code.\n\n---\n\n- `release_service.CreateNewTag` is called from the web router to handle creating a new tag, this function prepares a release struct with all the necessary information (every tag is stored as a release in the database).\n- `createTag` is then called which as first thing calls `LoadAttributes`.\n- `LoadAttributes` assumes the given release was loaded from the database and thus assumes the ID is non-zero. Loading 148026 attachments into this release.\n\nReviewed-on: https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14785\nReviewed-by: Andreas Ahlenstorf <redacted@example.invalid>\n",
      "author": {
        "actor": {
          "forge": "forgejo",
          "instance": "codeberg.org",
          "login": "Gusted",
          "id": "26734",
          "avatarUrl": "https://codeberg.org/avatars/44a59264e976fa585ed9f0a92abad9d7",
          "url": "https://codeberg.org/Gusted",
          "isBotHint": false
